  "description": "LEONARD WILSON KEENAN ESTATE & LETTING AGENTS  \nOur business is you....  \nTEAM DESMOND KEANY\n\nA BEAUTIFUL 1 BED / 1 BATH GROUND FLOOR HOME\nWELL PRESENTED THROUGHOUT\nHIGHLY SOUGHT AFTER REDBRICK COURTYARD DEVELOPMENT\nPERMIT PARKING AVAILABLE\n\nEARLY VIEWING STRONGLY ADVISED\n\nTeam Desmond Keany, the Dublin 8 Property Specialists, are truly delighted to present this charming home to the Dublin 8 market.\n\nRialto Court is one of the most historic and characterfilled developments in the South City, originally built in 1889 for Guinness Brewery workers and now firmly reestablished as one of Dublin’s most desirable urban neighbourhoods.\n\nNo. 79 is sure to impress firsttime buyers, professionals, investors and parties trading down alike.\n\nThe floor plan consists of: Entrance hall, dualaspect living / dining room, separate galley kitchen, shower room, primary bedroom and understairs storage.\n\nThe features of No. 79 include:\nModern fitted galley kitchen with subwaystyle tiling and excellent storage, fitted wardrobes in the primary bedroom, high ceilings, feature fireplaces, wooden & laminate flooring, fully tiled shower room with electric shower and doubleglazed windows to the front.\n\nThe property further boasts permit parking and an attractive redbrick facade.\n\nThe location is excellent making the city most accessible with every conceivable amenity on your doorstep.\n\n• Adjacent to the Luas Red Line with easy access to the Green Line\n• Minutes from Heuston Station, N4 & M50  \n• Convenient to South City & North City shopping\n• Close to New Crumlin Shopping Centre, Lidl & Tesco Express\n• Beside the New Children’s Hospital  \n• A short distance from The Liberties, NCAD, Griffith College & Trinity College\n• Near Royal Hospital Kilmainham, IMMA, Kilmainham Gaol & Guinness Brewery\n• Phoenix Park, Memorial Gardens, Liffey riverside walks & Greenway route to Chapelizod\n• Rialto Village offers cafés, restaurants, pubs, butchers, chemists & convenience stores\n\nNo. 79 offers complete charm, convenience and seclusion in the heart of Dublin 8.\n\nEarly viewing strongly advised.\n\n***All information provided is to the best of our knowledge. The utmost care and attention has been placed on providing factual and correct information. In certain cases, some information may have been provided by the vendor to us. We do not accept responsibility for mistakes, errors or inaccuracies in our online advertising and give each and every viewer the right to obtain an independent opinion on any concern they may have.***",
